00:24.000 --> 00:36.000
A cooling system transfers heat away from hot components and rejects it to the surroundings. Flow, area and temperature difference all matter.

00:36.000 --> 00:48.000
Draw a closed path from hot part through coolant and radiator to ambient air; arrows should form one continuous loop.

00:48.000 --> 01:00.000
Energy-flow map

01:00.000 --> 01:12.000
This ideal mechanism leaves out friction, temperature and part-specific behavior. Real designs need measurements.

